00:31:27.173 --> 00:31:28.130
it's not who I am.

00:31:28.130 --> 00:31:31.430
I just kind of separate myself from that,

00:31:31.430 --> 00:31:33.500
from that person and I just try to

00:31:33.500 --> 00:31:34.370
pretend like it didn't happen.

00:31:34.370 --> 00:31:35.940
Like I got money made,

00:31:35.940 --> 00:31:37.650
like, I can just, you know

00:31:38.940 --> 00:31:41.210
I'm sure it'll catch up with me someday,

00:31:41.210 --> 00:31:42.900
but right now I'm just trying to

00:31:44.130 --> 00:31:45.710
get through the day, like.

00:31:45.710 --> 00:31:48.250
I've never stole anything in my life

00:31:48.250 --> 00:31:49.880
and all of a sudden I'm
having to steal things

00:31:49.880 --> 00:31:51.670
because otherwise you know,

00:31:51.670 --> 00:31:54.560
I'm not gonna have it and I need it.

00:31:54.560 --> 00:31:58.320
You know, like I said, it's
just, it's a, it's a shitty

00:31:58.320 --> 00:31:59.640
it's a shitty life, you know?

00:31:59.640 --> 00:32:01.150
And I just,

00:32:01.150 --> 00:32:02.260
I need to,

00:32:02.260 --> 00:32:05.320
I need to start, doing the right thing and

00:32:05.320 --> 00:32:06.770
everyone's like, you need to go to rehab.

00:32:06.770 --> 00:32:09.510
And I just, I feel like
I'm not ready yet you know.

00:32:09.510 --> 00:32:12.710
I just, unfortunately, I'm not...

00:32:12.710 --> 00:32:15.330
- [Mark] Is your daughter with her father?

00:32:15.330 --> 00:32:17.050
- Yeah, she's with her dad

00:32:17.050 --> 00:32:18.980
and with my parents.

00:32:18.980 --> 00:32:22.980
And it just seems like
every time I try my hardest,

00:32:22.980 --> 00:32:25.540
it just there's something there

00:32:25.540 --> 00:32:27.230
to stop it and it's like,

00:32:27.230 --> 00:32:29.290
what the fuck am I supposed to do?

00:32:29.290 --> 00:32:32.040
Like, I've done everything you know.

00:32:32.040 --> 00:32:33.020
I just don't know.

00:32:33.020 --> 00:32:34.350
I don't, I just--.

00:32:34.350 --> 00:32:36.400
- [Mark] What do you think the core

00:32:36.400 --> 00:32:37.233
of your addiction is?

00:32:37.233 --> 00:32:38.410
Is it something that happened

00:32:38.410 --> 00:32:39.257
early in childhood, is--

00:32:39.257 --> 00:32:41.510
- I just think it's abandonment issues

00:32:41.510 --> 00:32:45.550
and it's not feeling like
I was important enough to,

00:32:45.550 --> 00:32:46.383
you know

00:32:48.030 --> 00:32:49.493
never being good enough.

00:32:50.400 --> 00:32:52.890
Always pushed to the side like,

00:32:52.890 --> 00:32:53.890
you know like

00:32:53.890 --> 00:32:55.910
what I have to say is
not important to anybody

00:32:55.910 --> 00:32:59.553
and nobody gives a shit about
your feelings, you know.

00:33:01.890 --> 00:33:03.490
Always having to rely on myself

00:33:03.490 --> 00:33:05.900
because I never had anybody to talk to.

00:33:05.900 --> 00:33:08.940
Like I see these families and
I'm just so envious, you know.

00:33:08.940 --> 00:33:11.690
And I just, I tell you know,

00:33:11.690 --> 00:33:14.980
little girl, whatever kid,
just be your age you know.

00:33:14.980 --> 00:33:16.460
Just live your,

00:33:16.460 --> 00:33:17.630
you know live you childhood.

00:33:17.630 --> 00:33:21.547
Like, don't be so quick
to grow up like you know.

00:33:21.547 --> 00:33:22.900
Cause you definitely could just,

00:33:22.900 --> 00:33:24.610
it goes so fast.

00:33:24.610 --> 00:33:26.020
And

00:33:26.020 --> 00:33:27.023
I just wish that,

00:33:29.010 --> 00:33:29.843
for my daughter's sake,

00:33:29.843 --> 00:33:30.803
I you know,

00:33:30.803 --> 00:33:34.240
I did cute things there
to keep her you know.

00:33:34.240 --> 00:33:35.090
I just hope that

00:33:36.570 --> 00:33:38.583
her dad and my parents you know they,

00:33:39.490 --> 00:33:40.630
they do say--

00:33:40.630 --> 00:33:41.960
- [Mark] Your daughter is seven now?.

00:33:41.960 --> 00:33:44.780
- Six, she's gonna be seven

00:33:44.780 --> 00:33:45.613
It breaks my heart

00:33:45.613 --> 00:33:47.090
I wasn't able to be there for her birthday

00:33:47.090 --> 00:33:50.313
or Christmas, and I just wanna I mean,

00:33:52.786 --> 00:33:55.379
there's nothing I could
say that would ever,

00:33:55.379 --> 00:33:56.212
you know--

00:33:56.212 --> 00:33:57.944
- [Mark] What do you think people

00:33:57.944 --> 00:33:58.990
- People think?

00:33:58.990 --> 00:34:00.590
- [Mark] That are not addicts,

00:34:00.590 --> 00:34:02.960
don't understand about addiction?

00:34:02.960 --> 00:34:06.220
- It's because we're,
it's emotional damage.

00:34:06.220 --> 00:34:08.013
It's PTSD really.

00:34:08.013 --> 00:34:11.023
It's just as bad maybe
if you'd gone to war.

00:34:12.050 --> 00:34:13.830
People put up with things
and see things that

00:34:13.830 --> 00:34:16.723
they just, it fucking shocks you

00:34:16.723 --> 00:34:18.490
and

00:34:18.490 --> 00:34:19.540
it's so

00:34:20.500 --> 00:34:21.890
upsetting to you,

00:34:21.890 --> 00:34:24.040
to your soul that, you
know, you block it out

00:34:24.040 --> 00:34:25.340
you block it out, block it out, and then,

00:34:25.340 --> 00:34:27.860
as you get older things
start re-surfacing.

00:34:27.860 --> 00:34:29.210
I mean the song play or

00:34:29.210 --> 00:34:30.355
you'll smell something and then just

00:34:30.355 --> 00:34:31.270
(fingers snaps).

00:34:31.270 --> 00:34:32.690
All of a sudden you're inch,

00:34:32.690 --> 00:34:35.460
up shit creek, no battle.

00:34:35.460 --> 00:34:36.630
And

00:34:36.630 --> 00:34:38.080
I think that

00:34:38.080 --> 00:34:39.352
a lot of people

00:34:39.352 --> 00:34:41.773
they're trying to self-medicate as well.

00:34:42.720 --> 00:34:45.100
For my depression, I use heroin.

00:34:45.100 --> 00:34:47.353
For weight loss, I use meth.

00:34:48.630 --> 00:34:49.880
That's about it you know.

00:34:51.110 --> 00:34:52.430
When you're addicted to heroin

00:34:52.430 --> 00:34:53.550
you're just trying to get enough

00:34:53.550 --> 00:34:54.620
so you could feel normal.

00:34:54.620 --> 00:34:56.092
- [Mark] That's the same
principle as alcohol, isn't it?

00:34:56.092 --> 00:34:58.570
- Yeah! same goes
- It is not different?

00:34:58.570 --> 00:34:59.403
right.

00:34:59.403 --> 00:35:00.860
Because it's anxiety.

00:35:00.860 --> 00:35:01.730
I think a lot of people,

00:35:01.730 --> 00:35:04.010
if they were given the right medication

00:35:04.010 --> 00:35:05.380
and they took it the right way

00:35:05.380 --> 00:35:06.520
and they were,

00:35:06.520 --> 00:35:08.300
I think they'd be a whole,

00:35:08.300 --> 00:35:09.570
in a whole different world.

00:35:09.570 --> 00:35:11.097
Because there are very
good people out here

00:35:11.097 --> 00:35:13.020
but they're also, you know

00:35:13.020 --> 00:35:15.910
the animals and the
bad, the bad, bad, bad.

00:35:15.910 --> 00:35:18.720
But, for the most part, I
just think that you know,

00:35:18.720 --> 00:35:19.650
people are just judgemental.

00:35:19.650 --> 00:35:20.620
It's okay to (fingers snaps)

00:35:20.620 --> 00:35:21.500
oh, well, you're a drug addict.

00:35:21.500 --> 00:35:23.860
Well, I wonder why, like, you know

00:35:23.860 --> 00:35:25.430
it's emotional pain, I think,

00:35:25.430 --> 00:35:28.360
and it's anxiety and just self-medication.

00:35:28.360 --> 00:35:29.750
Self-medicating.

00:35:29.750 --> 00:35:30.630
I don't think that they,

00:35:30.630 --> 00:35:32.650
they wanted to grow up
and say, and, you know

00:35:32.650 --> 00:35:34.770
be talking to themselves, you know

00:35:34.770 --> 00:35:36.470
on the corner in their tent.

00:35:36.470 --> 00:35:39.035
Like, I don't think that they wanted that.

00:35:39.035 --> 00:35:41.550
Personally, you know shit went down and

00:35:41.550 --> 00:35:45.280
they got fuck, their brain,
you know (beeps) like

00:35:45.280 --> 00:35:46.113
you know,

00:35:46.113 --> 00:35:46.946
did a,

00:35:46.946 --> 00:35:48.163
a 180.

00:35:49.270 --> 00:35:50.980
As I'm, you know,

00:35:50.980 --> 00:35:52.730
as here, I understand that

00:35:52.730 --> 00:35:55.440
And I can, I can relate and I don't judge

00:35:55.440 --> 00:35:57.300
and I accept everybody,

00:35:57.300 --> 00:35:59.910
but before and unless
you're in that situation

00:35:59.910 --> 00:36:01.380
unless you've gone through it,

00:36:01.380 --> 00:36:02.650
you're gonna, you know

00:36:02.650 --> 00:36:03.860
you're very quick to just be like,

00:36:03.860 --> 00:36:04.880
Oh, what a fucking loser?

00:36:04.880 --> 00:36:06.770
Like, I'll never be like that.

00:36:06.770 --> 00:36:08.270
Well, hopefully, you're not like that.

00:36:08.270 --> 00:36:10.800
But if you do end up like that,

00:36:10.800 --> 00:36:11.633
you know,

00:36:13.320 --> 00:36:14.790
he just,

00:36:14.790 --> 00:36:15.723
maybe I,

00:36:15.723 --> 00:36:16.820
I don't know.

00:36:16.820 --> 00:36:19.410
I think, I think it's sad

00:36:19.410 --> 00:36:20.440
because they're the first like I said

00:36:20.440 --> 00:36:22.350
they're the first people

00:36:22.350 --> 00:36:24.070
that will give you their
shirt off their back

00:36:24.070 --> 00:36:26.203
versus someone in you know,

00:36:27.100 --> 00:36:28.963
a family member even,

00:36:29.960 --> 00:36:31.300
a friend.

00:36:31.300 --> 00:36:34.260
I just think they know what it's like.

00:36:34.260 --> 00:36:35.093
You know they...

00:36:36.449 --> 00:36:38.610
You know, you never
know when it's gonna be

00:36:38.610 --> 00:36:39.780
your first day on the street.

00:36:39.780 --> 00:36:42.060
Like you're just supposed
to figure this out.

00:36:42.060 --> 00:36:42.893
Like you know,

00:36:42.893 --> 00:36:44.830
people are so scared to
death but I think that

00:36:44.830 --> 00:36:46.880
once you're able to survive

00:36:46.880 --> 00:36:48.180
and I think there's a lot of finessing

00:36:48.180 --> 00:36:50.230
a lot of manipulation,

00:36:50.230 --> 00:36:52.690
a lot of bartering.

00:36:52.690 --> 00:36:54.250
I think that you could survive anywhere.

00:36:54.250 --> 00:36:57.890
And I think it's, it made me stronger

00:36:57.890 --> 00:37:00.320
and I've able to find who I am.

00:37:00.320 --> 00:37:02.240
Maybe I needed that a little bit.

00:37:02.240 --> 00:37:03.830
Cause you know,

00:37:03.830 --> 00:37:06.930
when it going from like having stuff to

00:37:06.930 --> 00:37:09.080
to not having it and being
able to still be happy

00:37:09.080 --> 00:37:10.730
and survive and laugh through it,

00:37:12.170 --> 00:37:14.870
you know says something you know.

00:37:14.870 --> 00:37:16.280
I don't know what that is

00:37:16.280 --> 00:37:20.280
but there's a lesson
learned and I'm grateful.

00:37:20.280 --> 00:37:23.323
I'm grateful to be able to like,

00:37:24.650 --> 00:37:28.290
I can be, you know a chameleon really like

00:37:28.290 --> 00:37:29.960
be with people that have money,

00:37:29.960 --> 00:37:30.860
people that don't have money.

00:37:30.860 --> 00:37:32.210
I can fit in with everybody.

00:37:32.210 --> 00:37:34.310
Cause I've been in each stage.

00:37:34.310 --> 00:37:35.143
I feel like.

00:37:35.143 --> 00:37:36.710
So,

00:37:36.710 --> 00:37:37.950
I guess that's a

00:37:37.950 --> 00:37:40.050
you know one-up, I guess.

00:37:40.050 --> 00:37:40.883
But--

00:37:40.883 --> 00:37:42.710
- [Mark] Do you think
there's a chance that

00:37:42.710 --> 00:37:44.923
you might not get out of here?

00:37:44.923 --> 00:37:46.087
- No, I don't know.

00:37:46.087 --> 00:37:48.290
Shit, I ever thought about that.

00:37:48.290 --> 00:37:49.870
Well, I don't know.

00:37:49.870 --> 00:37:51.360
Some days I just wanna

00:37:51.360 --> 00:37:52.930
shoot myself in the face honestly.

00:37:52.930 --> 00:37:56.570
I just, sometimes I
walk around and I just,

00:37:56.570 --> 00:37:58.410
you know these people

00:37:58.410 --> 00:37:59.720
it's like the second coming of Jesus.

00:37:59.720 --> 00:38:02.280
I think I'm like the only
white girl here (chuckles).

00:38:02.280 --> 00:38:03.113
I don't know.

00:38:03.113 --> 00:38:04.610
The other ones are a little crazy.

00:38:04.610 --> 00:38:07.160
But sometimes I just I'm like,

00:38:07.160 --> 00:38:08.360
where the, where am I going?

00:38:08.360 --> 00:38:09.460
What should I do with myself?

00:38:09.460 --> 00:38:12.800
Why am I not going back to my career or

00:38:12.800 --> 00:38:13.990
or my,

00:38:13.990 --> 00:38:16.440
trying to work towards my family or why,

00:38:16.440 --> 00:38:17.560
you know, why this, why that?

00:38:17.560 --> 00:38:20.390
And then all of a sudden
I find myself high again

00:38:20.390 --> 00:38:23.320
and well, you know, I'll go tomorrow.

00:38:23.320 --> 00:38:24.230
I'll do this tomorrow,

00:38:24.230 --> 00:38:25.600
tomorrow, tomorrow, tomorrow.

00:38:25.600 --> 00:38:26.470
Well, I don't know.

00:38:26.470 --> 00:38:28.403
And, like I said, a couple weeks ago,

00:38:30.080 --> 00:38:31.810
I didn't know if tomorrow would have came.

00:38:31.810 --> 00:38:33.500
I ODed and I,

00:38:33.500 --> 00:38:34.620
and died and,

00:38:34.620 --> 00:38:35.750
luckily the people

00:38:35.750 --> 00:38:38.200
that were around me cared about me and

00:38:38.200 --> 00:38:40.020
they gave me Narcan

00:38:40.020 --> 00:38:41.840
and I took two of them.

00:38:41.840 --> 00:38:43.810
And then they, they did call 911.

00:38:43.810 --> 00:38:45.250
And even though they had guns

00:38:45.250 --> 00:38:47.010
and this and that and the other,

00:38:47.010 --> 00:38:49.810
they didn't, they put themselves
aside to save my life.

00:38:49.810 --> 00:38:51.710
And for that, I'll always be grateful.

00:38:52.820 --> 00:38:54.367
So you just never know.

00:38:54.367 --> 00:38:55.491
You just never know.

00:38:55.491 --> 00:38:57.660
I think it's important to
just live your life you know,

00:38:57.660 --> 00:38:59.450
and just be as happy as you can

00:38:59.450 --> 00:39:03.730
and do the right thing by
people and you know, and

00:39:03.730 --> 00:39:07.130
and, love more than, give love more than,

00:39:07.130 --> 00:39:09.603
Hey, you know at least try not to,

00:39:10.540 --> 00:39:11.890
you know,

00:39:11.890 --> 00:39:12.757
be an asshole

00:39:12.757 --> 00:39:14.160
(chuckles) really like you know,

00:39:14.160 --> 00:39:16.420
I think that I'm a giver.

00:39:16.420 --> 00:39:18.610
I just, I love to see if you can make

00:39:18.610 --> 00:39:20.180
you can be kind to somebody that you know,

00:39:20.180 --> 00:39:24.350
it could make their day
or their life, you know

00:39:24.350 --> 00:39:26.350
even taking a couple of
minutes out of your time

00:39:26.350 --> 00:39:27.610
to make them smile and laugh

00:39:27.610 --> 00:39:29.260
because they're always on edge you know,

00:39:29.260 --> 00:39:31.290
wondering if someone's
gonna get over on them,

00:39:31.290 --> 00:39:33.050
you know its, its,

00:39:33.050 --> 00:39:35.650
it's something that you
know is invaluable, I think.

00:39:36.920 --> 00:39:39.260
And they'll remember
you by that, you know?

00:39:39.260 --> 00:39:41.330
So I think you should be
remembered by you know,

00:39:41.330 --> 00:39:42.940
something good versus, (laughs)

00:39:42.940 --> 00:39:45.090
versus being an asshole
(laughs) to people.

00:39:46.007 --> 00:39:46.840
- [Mark] All right Heather

00:39:46.840 --> 00:39:47.950
Thank you so much for sharing your story.

00:39:47.950 --> 00:39:49.120
- Yeah. Thank you, thank you.

00:39:49.120 --> 00:39:49.953
- [Mark] Good luck in

00:39:49.953 --> 00:39:51.255
getting back together with your daughter.

00:39:51.255 --> 00:39:52.088
- Yes, thank you.

00:39:52.088 --> 00:39:52.921
- [Mark] Thanks.

